# `--dead` read a Haml template's Ruby as one run of text, so a `-#` comment's
# apostrophe ("it's") opened a string that swallowed the lines after it, and
# `= custom_banner` in a layout was never seen. And an `=` line ending in a
# comma continues on the next, whose names were not read at all. The index
# reads Haml now (DEC-658), and each is a call: the comment skipped, the
# continuation read.
dead app/helpers/widget_helper.rb WidgetHelper#custom_banner=single-caller~ WidgetHelper#hint_text=single-caller~ WidgetHelper#label_for=single-caller~ WidgetHelper#lonely=unreferenced~
